From 0bb159602386c26ed204fb19eaa3678bdeedd45a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 03:41:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 197/225] fix: the indirect light at a ray hit is the SVO's GI
 with occlusion, not the full probe

The two biggest terms in the energy ledger (audit errors 1 and 2, E1/E2/E3).

A surface seen DIRECTLY does not get the env probe's ambient at all: ApplyGI
mode 2 overwrites it with the SVO's GI (TiledShading.cfi:139-140), and then
SSDO multiplies that by occlDiff squared and the specular by
DeriveSpecularOcclusion. The same surface seen in a ray traced reflection was
getting the full probe irradiance instead, with occlusion hard-wired to (1,1) -
a different indirect model AND no occlusion at all. Unbounded in an interior lit
by a global probe; x1.7 to x5 more in any corner. Together they are why a
reflected wall reads brighter than the wall.

The hit now gets what the primary surface gets. TracingPS writes a fifth MRT,
HITGI (RGBA16F): .xyz = the SVO diffuse irradiance in the cell the hit came from
(RT_SampleVoxelIrradiance, unexposed, the same units TexGiDiffuse hands the
deferred consumer), .w = a voxel AO. It has to be produced there and not in
ShadePS, which may never touch a brick pool (t0-t3 aliasing). ShadePS reads it
at t37 and:

  - adds HITGI.xyz * PS_HDR_RANGE_ADAPT_MAX * AO to diffuseAcc - ApplyGI's own
    exposure multiply, happening where ApplyGI would have done it - before the
    energy split, so it picks up albedo * (1 - luminance(F0)) exactly as the
    deferred surfAlbedo does;
  - skips the probe DIFFUSE entirely, the way mode 2 replaces it;
  - multiplies the probe specular by a specular occlusion derived from HITGI.w
    through CE's own DeriveSpecularOcclusion and its max(ao*ao, 0.3) floor;
  - passes occlusion = (AO, specOcc) instead of (1, 1).

The AO is honest about what it is: three taps of brickPool_Opac along the hit
normal at 1.5, 3 and 4.5 voxels with 1/i falloff, projected onto the normal the
same way ConeTraceBrick does at CommonSVO.cfi:836. One ray, not a cone, and it
only sees the hit's own SVO cell because RT_VoxelBrickTC clamps at the cell
border. A hit with no cell, and every miss, writes (0,0,0,1) and is unchanged.

RT_SampleVoxelIrradiance's addressing is factored out into RT_VoxelBrickTC with
no change of arithmetic, so debug view 6 is byte-identical.

The target is allocated, bound as MRT 4 and read at t37 only under
e_svoTI_RT_Active; with the feature off nothing is allocated and the shader
parameters default to bUseHitGI = false, which is the old behaviour exactly.

